## 🎯 Final Thoughts

This solution is efficient and elegant:
- It leverages prefix sums (`left_sum`) and suffix sums (`right_sum`) in one pass.
- The parity check ensures we only count partitions with matching even/odd sums.
- Runs in linear time with constant space.

This pattern of **prefix-suffix tracking** is widely useful in problems involving balance, parity, or constraints between two halves of an array.  
